WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
Follow a crop from a farm, through
a trader's silo and a factory,

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.190
to a supermarket shelf.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.670
A few grain traders have been estimated
to handle up to 90 per cent of global

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.050
grain trade.

5
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.610
One transnational company, Unilever,
says its products are used by 3.7 billion

6
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.830
people every day.

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:25.150
The WTO, with 166 members,
deals with the rules of trade.

8
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.710
So who really decides what
ends up on your plate?

9
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.510
Farmers?

10
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.450
Governments?

11
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.510
Supermarkets?

12
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.330
Or you, the shopper?

13
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.570
In this mission, you'll map who
controls each stage of the food chain.

14
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.510
Then you'll test trade rules, aid,
food companies and supermarkets.

15
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.680
Your mission: judge who really
decides what ends up on your plate.
